Day 302/250:  Construct Product Matrix

Problem Statement #2906

Problem Statement Explantion:

Given a 0-indexed 2D integer matrix grid of size n x m, return a 2D matrix p of the same size, where p[i][j] is the product of all elements in the grid except for the element at grid[i][j].

Since the product can be very large, return the values modulo 12345.

Solution Approach:

The core challenge is to calculate the product of all elements except the current one without using division (since 12345 is not prime and the grid may contain zeros).
Linearization: We treat the 2D matrix as a single 1D sequence of length L=n×m.
Prefix Pass: We traverse the grid from top-left to bottom-right. At each cell (i,j), we store the product of all elements encountered before it in the result matrix p.
Suffix Pass: We traverse the grid in reverse (bottom-right to top-left). We maintain a running product of all elements encountered after the current cell and multiply it by the existing prefix product stored in p.
Modulo Arithmetic: To prevent integer overflow, we use long for the running product and apply % 12345 at every multiplication step

Here's the Code:

class Solution {
    public int[][] constructProductMatrix(int[][] grid) {
        int n = grid.length;
        int m = grid[0].length;
        int[][] p = new int[n][m];
        int MOD = 12345;
        
        long runningProduct = 1;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                p[i][j] = (int) (runningProduct % MOD);
                runningProduct = (runningProduct * (grid[i][j] % MOD)) % MOD;
            }
        }

        runningProduct = 1;
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            for (int j = m - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
                p[i][j] = (int) ((p[i][j] * runningProduct) % MOD);
                runningProduct = (runningProduct * (grid[i][j] % MOD)) % MOD;
            }
        }

        return p;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity: O(n×m)
Space Complexity: O(1)







